;; The soak: what the launcher runs when the queue is spent, each time with a fresh salt, so the
;; sims sample new worlds every run. Sims are the bug finders (about 50 worlds a second on one
;; runner, measured in smoke2); the gym walks landing set A once per goal to catch what only real
;; terrain shows. No issue: the report lands in the run's summary, and failures are pulled with
;; clojure -M:fleet pull --run <id>. Pushed (rather than launched) it runs unsalted. Ten workers,
;; not twenty: the soak leaves half the runners for pushes (tests and the gym) and dispatched
;; batches, which otherwise queue behind it for an hour or more.
{:fleet/label "soak"
 :fleet/workers 10
 :fleet/max-parallel 10
 :fleet/experiments
 [{:exp/name "forests" :exp/kind :sim :exp/property "forests" :exp/shards 8 :exp/worlds 2400000 :exp/est-s 6000}
  {:exp/name "wood" :exp/kind :gym :exp/goal "wood" :exp/runs 20 :exp/bots 2 :exp/est-s 180}
  {:exp/name "table" :exp/kind :gym :exp/goal "table" :exp/runs 20 :exp/bots 2 :exp/est-s 300}
  {:exp/name "pickaxe" :exp/kind :gym :exp/goal "pickaxe" :exp/runs 20 :exp/bots 2 :exp/est-s 360}]}
